  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am a content creator specifically on TikTok that focuses on content for Vrchat. I have more of a niche request that I know several other content creators would love to see included into the game by default.\nThere are ways to add camera movements via drone shots thanks to unity packages like VRCLens that work amazingly well to give footage I record a more cinematic touch. With how amazing a lot of the worlds people create are, providing cinematography with camera movements that I have complete control over gives what I create a more polished product.\nHere is a list of features I am essentially requesting to be included:\n-The ability to set multiple points for my camera to follow along a generated path between each point I add\n-Adjustments of speed with how fast the camera moves between points\n-Each point also saves depth of field settings\n-Allow this path to loop so you do not have to constantly reset it manually\n-Have a way to save these custom paths, can edit each point individually, and can import/export other paths.\n-A manual mode where I can move the camera manually with my controllers.\n-Settings for this manual mode where I can adjust the max speed, if I want to lock the camera on a certain plane, or if I want it to track around a given player or point in 3D space.\n-A portrait mode for stream mode cameras that is togglable.\n-Additional higher levels of stability when manually operating the vrc camera.\n-A HUD preview of the footage we are capturing that can be moved across our display and scaled appropriately.\n-The ability to lock depth of field focus on a specific player or point in 3D space.\nIf there's anything I missed, let me know :3",
